#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# algebraic_number

#% text
# `algebraic_number(theta, [c0, c1, ..., c(d-1)])` represents the element `c0 + c1 theta + ... + c(d-1) theta^(d-1)` of the number field `Q(theta)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The normal form has `theta` an algebraic integer: `root(g, k)` of its monic integer minimal polynomial `g` of degree `d` (a radical when `d = 2`), and exactly `d` rational coefficients, the polynomial reduced modulo `g`.

#% item
# A generator with a minimal polynomial of leading coefficient `a` becomes `a theta` (the coefficients `c_i` become `c_i/a^i`); an `algebraic_number` as the generator becomes the root of its minimal polynomial.

#% item
# A rational generator, or an element whose reduced polynomial is constant, gives the number itself; `n` gives the numerical value.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
algebraic_number(root(x => x^3 + x + 1, 3), [1, 2, 1])
#% output
#= algebraic_number(root(&(1 + &1 + &1^3), 3), [1, 2, 1])

#% cell
algebraic_number(3^(1/5), [1, 2, 1, 3, 3, 1])
#% output
#= algebraic_number(root(&(-3 + &1^5), 1), [4, 2, 1, 3, 3])

#% cell
algebraic_number(root(x => 5*x^5 + 11*x + 1, 1), [1, 1, 2])
#% output
#= algebraic_number(root(&(625 + 1375*&1 + &1^5), 1), [1, 1/5, 2/25, 0, 0])

#% cell
algebraic_number((1 + im)/2, [1, 3])
#% output
#= algebraic_number(1 + im, [1, 3/2])

#% cell
[algebraic_number(3, [1, 2]), algebraic_number(5/2, [3, 2])]
#% output
#= [7, 8]

#% cell
n(algebraic_number(sqrt(2)*im, [1, -1]), 30)
#% output
#= 1.000000000000000000000000000000000 - 1.4142135623730950488016887242096981im

#% cell
number_field_discriminant(algebraic_number(root(x => x^3 + x + 1, 3), [1, 2, 1]))
#% output
#= -31

